+
+## Runtime budgets, applied configuration, and later prerequisites
+
+Further observation found the trial's native absolute wall limit was 110s,
+ending missions despite real digging progress. The launch configuration now
+uses 180s without inventory/dimension progress and a 280s absolute ceiling;
+the plugin waits 295s, within its supported limit. Existing absolute-timeout
+tests still pass; selected runtime values are in `task-budgets-20261009.json`.
+
+The stop/start lifecycle also exposed a maintenance issue: writing the TOML
+file and calling the plugin reload entry left the host's applied snapshot at
+`unattended_enabled=false`. The runtime helper now uses the existing permanent
+`config/hot-update` API before the reload, and startup checks the plugin's
+actual enabled value. The isolated PowerShell regression failed before this
+change and passed afterward. No Neko platform source was changed. After
+application, `query-loop-effective-enabled-20261009.json` records a natural
+new mission, actual movement/inventory change, enabled unattended mode, and
+zero native kernel commits/handoff failures/tool caps during its 55s window.
+
+The body's later iron-mining attempts also had no suitable pickaxe. Native
+`mineOres` wrote this only to `progress.txt`, producing empty action feedback
+for its LLM. The skill now logs the missing prerequisite through the normal
+body output so the model can repair/craft a pickaxe instead of repeating a
+silent failure. Two red/green regressions cover absent and wooden-only picks;
+the full native suite now passes 225 tests (plugin remains 74). This skill is
+hot-reloaded, so it did not require another game restart. The body was observed
+checking inventory, attempting a crafting table, and choosing `getWood` after
+receiving the true missing-materials result. Its mining goal is not claimed
+complete.
+
+Final recovery observation was interrupted by a new external connection
+failure. The guardian is reconnecting, and an independent TCP probe to
+`micro.kangqiang.site:25702` (`60.176.65.106`) timed out after 8s. This confirms
+current unreachability from this host; the client's generic maintenance label
+does not prove that the server is actually under maintenance. Artifact:
+`server-connectivity-20261009.json`. At 10:51 the game had automatically
+reconnected: native login/spawn logs, fresh online telemetry, LAN viewer health,
+and the guardian's running state all confirmed recovery. The refreshed final
+health artifact distinguishes this later state from the earlier TCP timeout.
+Earlier action-recovery captures do not imply successful completion of the
+mining goal after that reconnect.
